<title>UK: Baltic, Black Sea oil exports up 0.3 mbpd on week.</title>
<headline>Baltic, Black Sea oil exports up 0.3 mbpd on week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil exports from Baltic and Black Sea terminals rose 304,582 barrels per day (bpd) in the first week of March to 2.05 million bpd, Petro-Logistics said.</p>
<p>This total is 695,502 bpd higher than the same week last year.</p>
<p>The Geneva-based consultancy, tracking tanker movements, said crude exports from Baltic and Black Sea ports rose 273,514 bpd on the week to 1.28 million bpd. This was 558,011 bpd above the same week last year.</p>
<p>Gas oil exports rose 20,318 bpd to 406,685 bpd but were still 129,171 below the same week a year ago.</p>
<p>Heavy fuel exports rose 25,392 bpd to 305,158 bpd and were 209,215 bpd over last year.</p>
<p>The following table provided by Petro-Logistics lists a breakdown in metric tonnes of petroleum exports from the Baltic and Black Sea in the fourth week of February.</p>
